{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/935149-tales-of-the-dark-eras-disscusion","id":935149,"title":"Tales of the Dark Eras Disscusion","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-21T11:16:11-07:00","id":935149,"title":"Tales of the Dark Eras Disscusion","content":"so, I've downloaded my copy and decided to use my spare time to read and discuses the fiction. Feel free to share your thoughts!<br /> <br /> As for now, I've finished the three first stories- and in the meanwhile, Unmanned is my favorite one. The Viking Era is a good time for a Beast game and the fiction showed it in a very interesting way, and I liked it that both the Begotten and the Hero got their place in the story. Plus, liked the ending, how it showed the influence of gender roles in the Viking Society and how it gave personality even for the minor characters. Plus, really loved the Changeling crossover. In sort, I really enjoyed reading it. Very well done.<br /> <br /> Bone and Gold was also nice one, although POV fictions are not really my style. The ending is really &quot;Dark Era&quot; style, with giving you a potential to tie things from the past into the present and even providing plot hooks allowing you to make an whole Chronicle around it. As for Hoarse.. well, that's problematic. From one side, it is really well written- it compelled you into keep reading on and on, as if the story is the Wheel itself while you are trapped in its endless turnings, an atmospheres strengthen by using it as POV. It is also very lyrical, even if the word &quot;shit&quot; shows up almost at every second sentence. The content itself, however, rubbed me completely the wrong way- while I don't mind hinting connection between God and the God Machine (hell, I did it myself more than once), stating outright &quot;your God is a cruel Machine and the Prophets are broken dolls manipulated by it&quot; really makes me uncomfortable. That is really weird considering that the one of the reasons that in &quot;To The Strongest&quot; there are no Hindu gods as Aeons was not to offend people who are part of that religion (at least, that was the answer I got in the forums). Sure, fictions are not considered &quot;canon&quot; usually- but it really made me feel uncomfortable reading it because it was so straight forward and uncompromising about the subject.<br /> <br /> Anyway, returning to read the book. I really hope for me interesting and exciting fictions :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-21T11:51:26-07:00","id":935170,"title":"","content":"Bone and Gold was worth the price of admission; it really nailed the feeling of the past as somewhere alien but familiar, and the whole thing was just brilliant.<br /> <br /> Dennis Detwiller's (I was amazed to see his name in the book!) story was also fantastic, even if I can't really tell what happened in it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T03:32:11-07:00","id":935501,"title":"","content":"so, I've finished reading the next three stories- Dry Spell, of Ravens and Roses and Suffering of the Unchosen. Among those three, Suffering was my favorite- I still liked Unmanned better, but it is a close tie with Bone and Gold. While it is a POV, the twist was nice and gave a lot of potential for a chronicle based around it. Eventually, the best fictions are more than just stories- but also give you material and inspiration to make a game around it, which both of those stories do. I also liked Ravens and Roses- it was really well written and gave a really good &quot;Changeling&quot; atmosphere, but the twist (while nice) still made me twitch because I really liked the main character. Dry Spell was written well- but I really didn't liked the main character. Mr Starling is annoying is hell, but I really liked how Ieldra was portrayed in the fiction. All in all, it was a really good Requiem story, even if I wouldn't have mind if the main character would be sent to meet the sunlight at the end :P<br /> <br /> In sort, for now my favorite is still Unmanned, with Bone &amp; Gold and Suffering of the Unchosen both sharing the very respected second place. I assume that by Sunday I'll finish the rest of the stories. Also, I must say I really like the fact that every story in here until now has a twist- it keeps you on the edge, and really allows you to feel the &quot;horror&quot; of the genre, especially since each twist really express the &quot;horror type&quot; of the gameline on which it's based. Also, I really like the fact that each of the fictions really has its own personality and fits the corresponding gameline's general atmosphere. And on an unrelated note- changelings! Changelings everywhere! :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T05:48:25-07:00","id":935546,"title":"","content":"O.O<br /> Okay, Ive been trying to search for that pdf you mentioned, but I can't seem to find it on the results.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>\u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/806810-deionscribe-s-homebrew-hub#post806810\" target=\"_blank\">&quot;My Homebrew Hub&quot;</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/828132-open-invite-age-of-azar\" target=\"_blank\">Age of Azar</a><br /> \u2022 <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/907224-the-kingdom-of-yamatai-dark-era\" target=\"_blank\">The Kingdom of Yamatai</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"",