nyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:51:15-07:00","id":935577,"title":"","content":"It is some kind of bonus- I've pledged only for Hunter and got it, so I assume that at least anyone of that level and above should have got it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T06:53:15-07:00","id":935579,"title":"","content":"Doesn't say. It wasn't a part of the Kickstarter, it was a special bonus. Presumably anyone who backed it.<br /> <br /> 'First off, here is a link to your complimentary copy of the Tales of the Dark Eras fiction anthology in PDF and other electronic formats. This is not something that you pledged for, nor was it part of the Dark Eras Kickstarter. We just wanted to say thanks for your patience as we've wrestled Dark Eras and it's Companion into being:'<br /> <br /> Some other info:<br /> <br /> 'The physical book version of the Tales of the Dark Eras fiction anthology will premiere exclusively at Gen Con in two weeks in Indianapolis and go on sale at DriveThruRPG.com a week after that.<br /> We will also having a special &quot;What is Dark Eras?&quot; panel at Gen Con on Saturday, August 6th, in the Crowne Plaza Grand Ballroom D, where we'll be answering questions, signing books including the Tales of the Dark Ages fiction anthology, and making a special announcement!<br /> The Prestige Edition Chronicles of Darkness Dark Eras book (the book this Kickstarter was all about) is slated to go to the printer in the next week, and the CofD Dark Eras Companion is being Art Directed.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T07:47:41-07:00","id":935598,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/935149-tales-of-the-dark-eras-disscusion?p=935579#post935579\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Doesn't say. It wasn't a part of the Kickstarter, it was a special bonus. Presumably anyone who backed it.<br /> <br /> 'First off, here is a link to your complimentary copy of the Tales of the Dark Eras fiction anthology in PDF and other electronic formats. This is not something that you pledged for, nor was it part of the Dark Eras Kickstarter. We just wanted to say thanks for your patience as we've wrestled Dark Eras and it's Companion into being:'<br /> <br /> Some other info:<br /> <br /> 'The physical book version of the Tales of the Dark Eras fiction anthology will premiere exclusively at Gen Con in two weeks in Indianapolis and go on sale at DriveThruRPG.com a week after that.<br /> We will also having a special &quot;What is Dark Eras?&quot; panel at Gen Con on Saturday, August 6th, in the Crowne Plaza Grand Ballroom D, where we'll be answering questions, signing books including the Tales of the Dark Ages fiction anthology, and making a special announcement!<br /> The Prestige Edition Chronicles of Darkness Dark Eras book (the book this Kickstarter was all about) is slated to go to the printer in the next week, and the CofD Dark Eras Companion is being Art Directed.'</div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, apparently any level of backing qualifies. I just had to dig through my emails to find the link. Downloading later...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Malkydel: &quot;And the Machine dictated; let there be adequate illumination.&quot;<br /> Yossarian: &quot;And lo, it was optimal.&quot;","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7212-vent0","name":"Vent0","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7212_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5184"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:26:55-07:00","id":935669,"title":"","content":"I've just downloaded mine. I've still not readed it, althought looking the index I'm a bit disappointed. I would have loved a neolithic fiction for mages or werewolves.<br /> <br /> I'm not saying I don't like it. As I've said, I've still not read it ad I've sure I'll enjoy it a lot. It's just a case about preferences. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>LAND OF THE DAMNED: SPAIN (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/3MHWYm\" target=\"_blank\">Land of the Damned: Spain</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/52b0TX\" target=\"_blank\">Kingdoms of Blood: Spain</a>; Cities of the Damned: <a href=\"https://goo.gl/XFMSSe\" target=\"_blank\">Barcelona</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/AXxdgq\" target=\"_blank\">Valencia</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/zkI5a1\" target=\"_blank\">Carthian Constitution</a> (1812), <a href=\"https://goo.gl/5H8M4s\" target=\"_blank\">Three Arrows Pact</a>: <br /> <br /> <b>OTHERS (Spanish): </b><a href=\"https://goo.gl/36HngB\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: The Redemption</a>, <a href=\"https://goo.gl/6B9V8l\" target=\"_blank\">Bloodlines: The Forgotten</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/247-uxas","name":"Uxas","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar247_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"394"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T10:53:11-07:00","id":935684,"title":"","content":"yeah- almost all of the fictions in the book are based around the original Dark Eras, with the exception of Unmanned (the Viking Era, because there is no &quot;original Beast Era&quot;), plus Hoarse (which is the time of the Latter Prophets) and No Signal (which is modern) which are not based around given Era. Perhaps if Dark Eras and the Companion would sell well, we may get more such anthologies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T16:19:07-07:00","id":935849,"title":"","content":"To be honest with you, I also didn't know this anthology was coming, but I'm loving it.<br /> <br /> I hope y'all love the Intro Fiction I wrote for the Beast chapter in the Companion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T19:34:08-07:00","id":935897,"title":"","content":"(It involves a child character, which I'm sure shocks no one given my record.)<br /> <br /> (No more spoilers.)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-size:12px\">-</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3093-hm8453a","name":"hm8453a","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3093_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"636"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-22T21:50:51-07:00","id":935936,"title":"","content":"That last story, &quot;No Signal&quot;. Damn. That's gonna stick with me.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><hr /><b>Social justice vampire/freelancer | He/Him</b><br /> <br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Actual Play:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/852858-vampire-the-requiem-%E2%80%93-bloodlines-ap\" target=\"_blank\">Vampire: The Requiem \u2013 Bloodlines</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Masquiem:</b></span> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/5268-13-licks-the-curses-of-caine-in-blood-smoke\" target=\"_blank\">Curses of Caine in Requiem 2nd</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#A52A2A\"><b>Storytellers Vault: </b></span><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=None%20More%20Dark%20Publishing#affiliate_id=321925\" target=\"_blank\">Author Page</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/192-yossarian","name":"Yossarian","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar192_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2297"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T06:18:41-07:00","id":936050,"title":"","content":"So, the sort review for my three daily stories- Cross Purposes, From Galveston and The Sea's Own.<br /> <br /> Cross Purposes started good, but the ending felt to me a bit lacking- I mean, I felt a really big build up through the fiction, but the ending itself was kinda anti climatic. It is not to say it was a bad fiction- it was good and well written, with developed characters and plot, but the finale was kinda &quot;meh&quot; compared to the rest of the stories.<br /> <br /> From Galveston was also not my cup of tea- it does give a good feeling of Promethean and the Dark Era, but it felt too &quot;bleak&quot; to me. Plus, my personal dislike for POVs, and again the ending was not as powerful as the other fictions. I did liked the conversations with &quot;Death&quot; and the portrayal of the life of a Promethean in general. Again, the story wasn't bad, but others were better.<br /> <br /> Now- The Sea's Own I really liked. It felt really &quot;geisty&quot; to me, and I enjoyed the fact the General was a lot more abstract than the usual Geist. The way that death is featured so heavily in the fiction without becoming &quot;dark and gloomy&quot; is really a part of Geist, and the fact the fiction resolve itself yet leaves taste for me is also enjoying. Plus, it gives you a plot hook for your games, which is always good- it takes the second place among my favorite fictions, right after Unmanned, and force me to break the tie between Gold and Bone and Suffering of the Unchosen for my top three. After some thought, Suffering defeats Gold and Bone simply because the plot hook it offers is much more founded for the Chronicle and how it expands one of the mysteries described in Doubting Souls directly (also, I already have thoughts about continuing the story- but I can't share them now because, you know, &quot;spoilers&quot;)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":503,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","user":"LostLight","date":". 07-23-2016, 01:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:07:42-07:00","id":936134,"title":"","content":"&quot;Galveston,&quot; not &quot;Glavestone.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-23T10:33:14-07:00","id":936145,"title":"","content":"fixed :P (need 10 characters)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T02:19:51-07:00","id":936467,"title":"","content":"so- finally finished the last three stories- and with it, the book itself.<br /> <br /> Let's start with the ending- No Signal. I get what people has talked about- that fiction was spooky as hell. It is nice to see how every fiction has its own writing style and how it works with the gameline it is meant to represent. As a pure Chronicles of Darkness fiction, I think it worked better than Hoarse- but I kinda hoped for it to be tied somehow to the past: after all, it is a part of Dark Eras. Instead, all modern (at least, from what I can gather). Still, spooky as hell.<br /> <br /> Top Dog was nice to read- while the twist wasn't as bombing as the ones in other books, I enjoyed it, which is nice considering that Bowery Dogs wasn't really my cup of tea, while the fiction brought it to life. I liked the fact the Pure in the story wasn't an &quot;evil caricature&quot; but a person- maybe a terrible person, but still a person. It was a good &quot;origin story&quot;, and actually I would have preferred it if more of the stories in the anthology were such origin stories.<br /> <br /> Now- for War Spoils: that fiction was awesome to read. Really, it gave a proper feeling for both Demon and the Dark Era, creating well developed characters and well written plot while being founded and expanding existing elements from the setting, creating plot hooks which could easily be used for the games. I liked the ending, and the fact the story focused around supernatural characters as the main characters instead of mortals/secondary actors who just fall into a plot which is not their own. In sort- well done<br /> <br /> Now, after finishing the Anthology, I can finally choose my top 3 favorite stories- Unmanned keeps the 1st place from almost the beginning as my favorite. War Spoils, who showed up near the end rise up and steals the 2nd place. That leaves Sea's Own with the respectful 3rd place. The other stories were also good and interesting, of course- but I still don't like Hoarse. I can't but feel uncomfortable when I read it.<br /> <br /> Of course, with so many characters in the stories, my favorite ones should also be mentioned. Alva is clearly my favorite one, and Belle taking the second place, while the third belongs to the General. All in all, I liked the book and I'm really happy that Onyx Path decided to give it to anyone who backed the project as a special bonus. Now- I'm going back to wait for the Companion :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T03:58:11-07:00","id":936486,"title":"","content":"Have all backers already gotten the link? I at least have not seen anything yet, and am a bit jealous of those people who already have the book.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/304-penta","name":"Penta","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar304_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"617"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T17:15:00-07:00","id":936809,"title":"","content":"The link was in an update to the Kickstarter, so if you go to the KS page and check the updates, you should be able to get the link (the update is backers only, of course).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13-blackhatmatt","name":"blackhatmatt","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar13_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"464"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-24T18:17:06-07:00","id":936829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>LostLight</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/935149-tales-of-the-dark-eras-disscusion#post935149\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The content itself, however, rubbed me completely the wrong way- while I don't mind hinting connection between God and the God Machine (hell, I did it myself more than once), stating outright &quot;your God is a cruel Machine and the Prophets are broken dolls manipulated by it&quot; really makes me uncomfortable. That is really weird considering that the one of the reasons that in &quot;To The Strongest&quot; there are no Hindu gods as Aeons was not to offend people who are part of that religion (at least, that was the answer I got in the forums). Sure, fictions are not considered &quot;canon&quot; usually- but it really made me feel uncomfortable reading it because it was so straight forward and uncompromising about the subject.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's a rather huge gulf between &quot;a story told by a horrifying amalgamated victim-instrument of the God-Machine hits on a lot of similar notes to stories of the Biblical prophet&quot; and &quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/385943-dark-eras-chapter-to-the-strongest?p=524898#post524898\">there are limits to how comfortable Malcolm Sheppard is</a> with presenting a game statement that the thread's context made clear was easy to misinterpret as '<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/385943-dark-eras-chapter-to-the-strongest?p=525938#post525938\">Shiva is a stattable entity in the Chronicles of Darkness</a>' when lack of direct presentation of a Hindu-mythology-sourced most common form <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/385943-dark-eras-chapter-to-the-strongest?p=527260#post527260\">does nothing to remove the Aeons' nature as beings who wear many faces</a>.&quot;<br /> <br /> Something verbally sharing a history that sounds broadly like the tale of the Prophet Jonah with memories that sound broadly like the tale of the Prophet Elijah and so on up the chain with occult mechanical apparatuses worked into the changeover point is not on par with saying that the being Hinduism describes as the destroying aspect of the formless supreme God is a common face for an entity that presides over one or two of the Arcana that describe reality.<br /> <br /> Also no &quot;outright statement&quot; happens.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-25T00:28:02-07:00","id":936970,"title":"","content":"potential spoilers for Hoarse:<br /> <br /> <div style=\"margin: 5px 20px 5px 20px;\"> <div style=\"margin-bottom:2px; font-size: 80%;\"> <input type=\"button\" value=\"Spoiler\" style=\"width:45px;font-size:10px;margin:0px;padding:0px;\" onClick=\"if (this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display != '') { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = ''; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Hide'; } else { this.parentNode.parentNode.getElementsByTagName('div')[1].getElementsByTagName('div')[0].style.display = 'none'; this.innerText = ''; this.value = 'Show'; }\" /> </div> <div style=\" margin: 0px; padding: 6px; border: 3px groove blue; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px; -webkit-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); -moz-box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75); box-shadow: 1px 1px 5px rgba(50, 50, 50, 0.75);\"> <div style=\"display: none;\"><div style=\"background: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.8); padding: 6px; -webkit-border-radius: 10px; -moz-border-radius: 10px; border-radius: 10px;\">That's not &quot;something which broadly resemble&quot; the story of the Prophets. This is almost identical to the stories of the Prophets. There are few changes, buy there is not &quot;unreliable narrator&quot; in the way the story is presented, because trusting the Prophet's story is very important to the fiction itself. If you decide that the Prophet lies, then the story lose much of its horror. If you decide he said something which is mostly true- than the consequences are not comfortable for me, because it should either mean that somehow all the instances of not merely one Prophet, but almost all of them, were &quot;copied&quot; by the machine or that all the Prophets were its instruments. It is not some weird book with strange story- it is meant to be a person who experienced the events first hand telling what happened. Again, I'm not saying that the writing was anywhere near bad- it was good, really good- and you could see that the writer either did his research or knew the subject closely. All I'm saying is that the fiction requires too much of suspension of disbelief for both enjoying the story AND deciding that what the Prophet say is mostly not true- too much for it to be worth it, for me.<br /> <br /> Again, I'm not saying anything like &quot;this fiction is EVIL burn it and hate it&quot;. I'm saying that it would have been better, IMO, that the nature of such beings would be kept at least partly mysterious and hidden. People have their right to enjoy that fiction and I don't have a problem with that- I'm just saying that I really, really didn't liked it because of the content which had me too chose, while reading, between enjoying an awesome story and feeling hurt because of personal believes, and what can I say? Personal believes win :P</div></div> </div> </div>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://www.storytellersvault.com/browse.php?author=Shachar%20Gold\" target=\"_blank\">Check my STV content</a>, <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/28219-my-weekly-wod-project-program\" target=\"_blank\">Or My Homebrew</a><br /> <br /> &quot;And all our knowledge is, Ourselves to know&quot;- An Essay on Man<br /> <br /> I now blog in <a href=\"https://chroniclesoflostlight.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">here</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/503-lostlight","name":"LostLight","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar503_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4531"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T09:24:01-07:00","id":938165,"title":"","content":"That was a really enjoyable collection and a pleasant surprise. To be honest, I felt that &quot;Unmanned&quot; was the weakest story of the group; it was exactly what you'd expect from a Beast story, with no particularly interesting twists. Eirik's narmy ejaculation of bigotry during the climax also killed the mood for me--we can feel okay that he dies because the man living in Viking-era Scandinavia has the Bad Politics. I think Beast just needs more stories told for it to find its footing; you have to get through all the predictable tales before you can break out the really fun stuff.<br /> <br /> I enjoyed the bizarre, repetitious nature of &quot;Hoarse.&quot; It also made me rethink the God-Machine a little, and how to use It in Chronicles of Darkness stories. &quot;No Signal&quot; was great too, though I was uncertain if there was meant to be G-M influence there as well. One line near the beginning kind of implied it, but then it never really came up again. The drainpipe scene was nice and creepy.<br /> <br /> I loved &quot;War Spoils,&quot; but then again, there has yet to be a piece of Demon fiction that I haven't loved.<br /> <br /> &quot;Suffering of the Unchosen&quot; was probably the most interesting story of the bunch, in my opinion. I had to read it a few times to get what was going on. I'm glad that Valentinelli tied in those weird corpses from the Salem chapter of <i>Dark Eras</i>. The way the ending was written also reminded me of works of fiction that were actually written in Puritan times. (Maybe anyway. I'm actually having a hard time coming up with solid examples, so maybe it's just a trick of the light. It does harken back to something though. &quot;The Devil and Daniel Webster&quot;? Not really the same thing.)<br /> <br /> Thank you for this, Richard Thomas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1423-espritdecalmar","name":"espritdecalmar","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1423_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"941"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}